  "structural_blocker_diagnosis": {
    "summary": "8 of the 218 findings, on 7 nodes, cannot be cleared by re-attestation, by editing a record (forbidden), or by any act that is not a source edit.",
    "mechanism": "_attestation_staleness skips a record only when EVERY (node_id, capability_id) pair it holds is owned by a later record (`all(winner.get(pair) != idx ...)`). These 7 live records each hold at least one pair whose capability_id is no longer in the node's `requires`, so a replacement packet -- which attester_packets.build() derives FROM `requires` -- can never take ownership of it. The predecessor therefore stays in the freshness pass permanently and re-reports its finding.",
    "orphan_capability_ids": [
      "orally",
      "given_orally",
      "arts",
      "rhythmic_properties",
      "visual_elements"
    ],
    "measured": "Each of those five ids appears in NO node's `requires` anywhere in the tree and in NO CAPABILITY_PROVIDERS entry. They are consulted by nothing: _validate_attestation iterates `requires` only. They are words the human-authored `requires_ignore` ground truth (data/skeletons/requires_ignore.lock.json) marks as named by MATATAG but deliberately not provided -- oral delivery and arts integration.",
    "why_it_matters_beyond_these_7": "This is not a G1-3 artifact. Any future grade in which a competency's `requires_ignore` grows, or a `requires` id is renamed after attestation, inherits a permanently un-clearable finding. capability_phase2 can then never reach 0, which in turn keeps the three \u00a76F mutations at INVALID and assertion_coverage_8 red -- so the Definition of Done is blocked by it.",
    "candidate_fix_NOT_APPLIED": "In the supersession test, disregard verdict pairs whose capability is not in the node's current `requires`, because such a pair is a ruling no check consults -- which is the rationale _attestation_staleness's own docstring already gives for skipping fully-superseded records. A record all of whose CONSULTED pairs are superseded is not evidence for anything.",
